// Title: Setup16.EXE Execution With Custom .Lst File
// Sigma ID: 99c8be4f-3087-4f9f-9c24-8c7e257b442e
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: frack113
// Date: 2024-12-01 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, persistence, execution, stealth, T1574.005
// Description: Detects the execution of "Setup16.EXE" and old installation utility with a custom ".lst" file.
//   These ".lst" file can contain references to external program that "Setup16.EXE" will execute.
//   Attackers and adversaries might leverage this as a living of the land utility.
// False positives:
//   - On modern Windows system, the "Setup16" utility is practically never used, hence false positive should be very rare.
// References:
//   - https://www.hexacorn.com/blog/2024/10/12/the-sweet16-the-oldbin-lolbin-called-setup16-exe/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_setup16_custom_lst_execution.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (InitiatingProcessFolderPath =~ "C:\\Windows\\SysWOW64\\setup16.exe" and InitiatingProcessCommandLine contains " -m ") and (not(FolderPath startswith "C:\\~MSSETUP.T\\"))
